From 547da80acc7718e3391a3df720b7ce90bc3b6234 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 05yuki <ceu.azul.samu@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:44:34 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] gpu-moe-fp32: GPU MXFP4 experts in the checkpoint's layout,
 rounded once (Triton)

The GPU-resident MXFP4 experts in fp32 glue. `SGLANG_MXFP4_MOE_FP32=1`
(with `--moe-runner-backend marlin`) replaces the Marlin MoE method with
`Mxfp4Fp32MoEMethod` (`mxfp4_fp32_moe.py`): Triton kernels that read the
checkpoint's MXFP4 layout and round to bf16 once, at the weighted sum;
decode uses a per-route GEMV, larger batches the tensor cores on the
routes with a weight. When the experts run through Marlin instead,
`SGLANG_MARLIN_MOE_FP32_GLUE=1` keeps the steps around Marlin's two
GEMMs in fp32.

Numerics: Not bit-identical to Marlin: fewer bf16 roundings, closer to
an fp32 reference. The fp32 MoE repeats bit for bit from launch to
launch.

Prerequisites: none; applies alone on tier 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C2UBZdnrDZSBh8yQz8rc9g
